  "notes": "Single-staff melody with two stacked verses. Verse 1 has one syllable fewer than verse 2 in line 3 (\"trem-_-bling\" vs \"bow down their heads\"): bar 6 beat 3 (c''8) carries a verse-2 syllable (\"their\") but NO verse-1 syllable. The final melisma \"pass-ing _\" is slurred in both verses. DAMAGE (crop): Image edges cut through the staves. Mild: tight crop 0.4 mm outside the staff ends (braces/brackets cut off), header kept. Scan: header (title/credits) cropped away, 0.8 mm cut into the staff starts and 3.0 mm off the staff ends (end barlines gone). Severe: cut 1.49 mm into the staff starts (up to just before the first clef / part name / lyric) and 8.61 mm off the ends (to just after the right-most notehead/stem/lyric). Cut amounts are computed per page from the clean raster so that no clef, key/time signature, notehead, stem, accidental, lyric or part name is removed - only staff-line ends, brackets/braces, barlines and the header. TRUTH LIMITATIONS: Barlines at system starts/ends (incl. the final barline) are partly or completely cut off - they are still present in the truth. scan/severe: title/composer/poet header text is not visible; ignore work-title/creators when scoring."
